// ==============================================================================
// File: tests/test3_syntax_error.toy
// Purpose: Negative test verifying compiler syntax error detection and reporting.
//
// What it Tests:
//  - Intentionally invalid syntax: consecutive binary operators ('+ *') and
//    a missing terminating semicolon.
//  - Confirms that Bison's yyerror() triggers with an accurate line number.
//  - Confirms that the compiler exits gracefully with code 1 without crashing.
// ==============================================================================

a = 2 + * 3;
print(a)
